{"id": "q0071", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2469925657, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "A small sunflower has 3 dozen seeds and a large sunflower has 50% more seeds than a small sunflower.  How many sunflower seeds are there altogether?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0071.wav", "input_sha256": "d8a31a8e8988315081f6690903fece10c0852c17aca5833d9ea7db178fe30aec", "input_samples": 209200, "input_s": 13.075, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.0602, "act": 0.999, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "A small sunflower has 3 dozen seeds, which is 3 times 12, equal ing 36 seeds. A large sunflow er has 50% more, so that's 0.5 times 36 equals 1 8 more seeds. Add ing those gives us 36 plus 18, which is 54 seeds for the large one. To get the total, add the small and large together: 3 6 plus 54 equals 90. So there are 90 sunflower seeds altogether.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 25, "feed_lag_max_ms": 72, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 103, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0071_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "0d607e458d27a6cd79e7fd5ad112172691acaca3177d138b642bd6dd972d1a9d", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 25.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.079, 1.143, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.079, 2.143, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.085, 3.153, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.081, 4.146, 1, 0, 0