{"id": "q0084", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1691024217, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Nate's dog can dig six holes a day. He digs for 14 days while Nate is on vacation. When Nate gets home, he starts filling in 9 holes a day, but the dog keeps digging 6 new holes every night. How many weeks does it take him to fill in all the holes?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0084.wav", "input_sha256": "801345e684994fb9e7a62d3fe5ad11a2988b08bc6c4ce452c3e3dc36db5090f4", "input_samples": 313000, "input_s": 19.562, "n_real_chunks": 20, "score": 0.3561, "act": 0.9986, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so the dog digs 6 holes a day for 14 days while Nate is on vacation. That' s 6 times 1 4, which is 84 hole s. Then, when Na te gets home, he fills in 9 holes a day, but the dog keeps digging 6 new holes every night. So each day, Net t loss is 9 minus 6, which is 3 holes. To fill in 84 holes at a rate of 3 holes per day, we divide 8 4 by 3. That gives us 28 days. Now, to find how many weeks that is, we divide 28 by 7. That equals 4. So it takes him 4 weeks to fill in all the holes.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 19, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 36, "feed_lag_max_ms": 137, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 739, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0084_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "b2f3e6