{"id": "q0125", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3907012978, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "The equation\n\\[x^{10}+(13x-1)^{10}=0\\,\\]has 10 complex roots $r_1,$ $\\overline{r}_1,$ $r_2,$ $\\overline{r}_2,$ $r_3,$ $\\overline{r}_3,$ $r_4,$ $\\overline{r}_4,$ $r_5,$ $\\overline{r}_5,$ where the bar denotes complex conjugation. Find the value of\n\\[\\frac 1{r_1\\overline{r}_1}+\\frac 1{r_2\\overline{r}_2}+\\frac 1{r_3\\overline{r}_3}+\\frac 1{r_4\\overline{r}_4}+\\frac 1{r_5\\overline{r}_5}.\\]\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0125.wav", "input_sha256": "1f52f81768ca778d1c9c32eca86e9b0e0335d7d7143914cec4d9a3689828ce13", "input_samples": 499200, "input_s": 31.2, "n_real_chunks": 32, "score": 0.9585, "act": 0.9963, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Assuming the equation is \\[ x^{10}+13x^5+10=0, \\] let \\(y=x^5\\).", "expert_answer": "Assuming the equation is\n\n\\[\nx^{10}+13x^5+10=0,\n\\]\n\nlet \\(y=x^5\\). Then\n\n\\[\ny^2+13y+10=0.\n\\]\n\nSo\n\n\\[\ny=\\frac{-13\\pm \\sqrt{129}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThus the roots split into two groups of 5, with moduli\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{13+\\sqrt{129}}2\\right)^{1/5}\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n\\left(\\frac{13-\\sqrt{129}}2\\right)^{1/5}.\n\\]\n\nFor each conjugate pair \\(r,\\overline r\\),\n\n\\[\nr\\overline r=|r|^2.\n\\]\n\nSo\n\n\\[\n\\frac1{r\\overline r}=\\frac1{|r|^2}.\n\\]\n\nThere are 5 roots from each \\(y\\)-value, so the requested sum over conjugate pairs is half the sum over all 10 roots:\n\n\\[\n\\frac52\\left[\\left(\\frac{13+\\sqrt{129}}2\\right)^{-2/5}\n+\n\\left(\\frac{13-\\sqrt{129}}2\\right)^{-2/5}\\right].\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac52\\left[\\left(\\frac{2}{13+\\sqrt{129}}\\right)^{2/5}\n+\n\\left(\\frac{2}{13-\\sqrt{129}}\\right)^{2/5}\\right]}\n\\]", "transcript": "The equation x ten plus thirteen i times one ten equals zero has ten complex roots r one overline one r two, overline r two r three, overline r three r four, overline r four r five, overline r five, where the bar denotes complex conjugation. Find the value of frac one one overline r one plus frac on", "asr_s": 4.82, "expert_s": 32.81, "expert_input_samples": 499200, "expert_input_s": 31.2, "expert_input_sha256": "1f52f81768ca778d1c9c32eca86e9b0e0335d7d7143914cec4d9a3689828ce13", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 33.08, "relay_synth_ms": 12123, "onset_chunk": 31, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 3496, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 3496, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_conservative_relay.wav", "sha256": "86f210bf55be0e65f4f837557d36e2b00b91716f6f82c6c5c374b4d1cf575f00", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 20.92}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_conservative_candidate.wav", "sha256": "e04e37dae7109b01550196ae53ffba451b208c794c686b5c4ad97ecfadce0c15", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_conservative_stall.wav", "sha256": "aa741cc17b9b9248816c713eb4bbb639ecd19dda57d410da65b049da03c260b7", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.079, 1.143, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.081, 2.145, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.08, 3.142, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.084, 4.156, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.081, 5.147, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.079, 6.143, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.083, 7.146, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.083, 8.148, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.081, 9.147, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.083, 10.148, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.085, 11.151, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.085, 12.151, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.085, 13.152, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.087, 14.156, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.09, 15.159, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.087, 16.155, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.087, 17.155, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.087, 18.155, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.087, 19.153, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.086, 20.152, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.082, 21.144, 1, 0, 0], [21, 1, 22.0, 22.087, 22.154, 1, 0, 0], [22, 1, 23.0, 23.089, 23.156, 1, 0, 0], [23, 1, 24.0, 24.086, 24.152, 1, 0, 0], [24, 1, 25.0, 25.086, 25.151, 1, 0, 0], [25, 1, 26.0, 26.089, 26.157, 1, 0, 0], [26, 1, 27.0, 27.084, 27.148, 1, 0, 0], [27, 1, 28.0, 28.087, 28.151, 1, 0, 0], [28, 1, 29.0, 29.088, 29.153, 1, 0, 0], [29, 1, 30.0, 30.095, 30.17, 1, 0, 0], [30, 1, 31.0, 31.086, 31.153, 1, 0, 0], [31, 1, 31.2, 31.287, 32.011, 0, 24000, 0], [32, 0, 32.2, 35.778, 36.565, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 31.2, "last_real_feed_done": 31.287, "onset": 32.011, "gate_read_done": 32.011, "fire": 32.011, "candidate_first_pcm": 32.011, "stall_note": 32.014, "stall_first_pcm": 35.696, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 36.565, "expert_req": 32.013, "expert_resp": 69.645, "relay_synth_start": 69.646, "relay_first_pcm": 70.579, "relay_synth_end": 81.77, "first_any_pcm": 32.011, "first_answer_pcm": 70.579, "session_end": 83.153}, "ttfa_answer_s": 39.379, "ttfa_any_s": 0.811}
{"id": "q0152", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 969230870, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "The value of the coefficient K_G in a wetted wall column forthe absorption of SO_2 in air by water at 70°F is 0.068lbmol/hr \\bulletsqft\\bullet atm.The resistance of gas and liquid filmsare equal in the absorption of SO_2. The diffusivities of SO_2 and NH_3 at 49°F are 0.115 and 0.168 cm^2/sec, respectively. Find the value of for the absorption of NH_3 in waterat 49°F when all other conditions are the same.\n\nA. 0.085lbmol/hr sqft atm\nB. 0.05lbmol/hr sqft atm\nC. 0.188lbmol/hr sqft atm\nD. 0.174lbmol/hr sqft atm\nE. 0.16lbmol/hr sqft atm\nF. 2.428lbmol/hr sqft atm\nG. 0.068lbmol/hr sqft atm\nH. 0.210lbmol/hr sqft atm\nI. 0.135lbmol/hr sqft atm\nJ. 0.092lbmol/hr sqft atm\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0152.wav", "input_sha256": "5bc334acc43549a5dad6d15216ed7e1ffbcbfbce19b3c814c0341b9020538699", "input_samples": 893400, "input_s": 55.837, "n_real_chunks": 56, "score": 0.8922, "act": 0.9983, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so we' re given the value of kG for SO2 absorption in a wetted wall column at 70°F, which is 0.0 68 pound-mole per hour-sq ft-atom. We also know that the resistances of gas and liquid films are equal, meaning it's a control-limiting step situation. The de ffusivities for SO2 and NH 3 at 49°C are 0. 115 and 0. 16 8 cm²/s, respectively. Since temperature is similar, we can use these values to compare the kG values proportionally based on diffusivity. For gases absorb ing in liquids with film resistance controlling, the kG value is approximately proportional to the square root of the diffusivity when other conditions like temperature and physical properties are similar. So if I take the ratio of the kG for N H3 over the kG for SO2, it should be roughly the square root of the ratio of their de ffusivities. Let me calculate that: s q rt of 0.1 68 divided by 0.115. That gives me about 1. 23. So the new kG for NH3 would be 0.0 68 times 1.2", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 56, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 63, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 387, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0152_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "6431dc56799356e363ef2c8490b2d54bfe5ea6cf33dd11b1fe4715b574885076", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 60.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.078, 1.143, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.079, 2.142, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.081, 3.148, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.082, 4.15, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.081, 5.147, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.08, 6.147, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.081, 7.15, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.082, 8.15, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.08, 9.145, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.083, 10.151, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.083, 11.151, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.084, 12.151, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.084, 13.151, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.086, 14.154, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.095, 15.173, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.101, 16.177, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.121, 17.199, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.13, 18.21, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.11, 19.195, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.115, 20.196, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.102, 21.18, 1, 0, 0], [21, 1, 22.0, 22.115, 22.197, 1, 0, 0], [22, 1, 23.0, 23.098, 23.184, 1, 0, 0], [23, 1, 24.0, 24.103, 24.182, 1, 0, 0], [24, 1, 25.0, 25.098, 25.179, 1, 0, 0], [25, 1, 26.0, 26.094, 26.167, 1, 0, 0], [26, 1, 