{"id": "q0175", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2509749559, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "At the outset of group counseling, the therapist should explain char the obligation of the group member to respect confidentiality is\n\nA. on the “honor system” only\nB. protected by state/provincial laws\nC. less of an issue than it is in individual therapy\nD. mandated by federal law\nE. the legal responsibility of the therapist\nF. only applicable to the therapist\nG. only necessary if sensitive information is shared\nH. dependent on the group's consensus\nI. not applicable in group settings\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0175.wav", "input_sha256": "fa5307afe910cd5a70f553f4778be5ff4ea9f094ac909086fecdea4e2950b2ed", "input_samples": 541800, "input_s": 33.862, "n_real_chunks": 34, "score": 0.4509, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The correct answer is B. Pro tected by state or provincial laws. In group counsel ing, just like in individual therapy, client confidential ity is protected by legal standards that vary by jurisdiction. This obligation to maintain confidentiality is not limited to the therapist alone but extends to all group members as a matter of professional and ethical responsibility.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 33, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 24, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag