{"id": "q0201", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3757920688, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Statement 1| Layer Normalization is used in the original ResNet paper, not Batch Normalization. Statement 2| DCGANs use self-attention to stabilize training.\n\nA. Statement 2 is True, but it's not clear about Statement 1\nB. Statement 1 and 2 are both partially true and partially false\nC. Statement 1 is False, but it's not clear about Statement 2\nD. False, True\nE. Statement 1 is True, but it's not clear about Statement 2\nF. True, True\nG. Statement 2 is False, but it's not clear about Statement 1\nH. True, False\nI. Both Statements are unclear\nJ. False, False\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0201.wav", "input_sha256": "c07497db68f5f5ad10653bf0a991f8a034ddb41b8fe003af41f98ff9991a73ae", "input_samples": 633000, "input_s": 39.562, "n_real_chunks": 40, "score": 0.7224, "act": 0.9967, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "That's false, false. Statement 1 is false because batch normal ization was used in the original ResNet paper, not layer normalization. And statement 2 is also false; DC- GANs do not use self- attention to stabilize training—they typically rely on techniques like spectral nor malization or weight clipping for stability.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 39, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 18, "feed_lag_max