{"id": "q0218", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3208304725, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Which of the following is not correct for the perfectly competitive firm, in the long run?\n\nA. price = marginal revenue.\nB. price = minimum average cost.\nC. price = minimum average variable cost.\nD. price = marginal cost.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0218.wav", "input_sha256": "808655640e3b5a30df6a8bd7fc962ff3c6835ccaf2b314684b6a92eba795735f", "input_samples": 267400, "input_s": 16.712, "n_real_chunks": 17, "score": 0.481, "act": 0.9997, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "C, price equals minimum average variable cost is not correct for the perfectly competitive firm in the long run. In the long run, a perfectly competitive firm will produce at the level where price equals marginal cost and also equal minimum average total cost, which includes both fixed and variable costs. The condition that price equals minimum average variable cost relates more to short-run decisions about whether to continue operating or shutting down rather than the long-run equilibrium condition.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 16, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 18, "feed_lag_max_ms": 338, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 802, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0218_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "2a06a298efe766a8d51a056329c7d125e1540ad78ba6fb7f8369ce6989c150df", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 18.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.078, 1.142, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.077, 2.136, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.083, 3.146, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.074, 4.133, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.083, 5.15, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.077, 6.14, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.08, 7.142, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.083, 8.148, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.083, 9.149, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.079, 10.142, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.08, 11.142, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.081, 12.14, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.085, 13.151, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.083, 14.143, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.077, 15.136, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.078, 16.135, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 16.712, 16.787, 17.268, 0, 24000, 0], [17, 0, 17.712, 17.792, 18.461, 0, 24000, 0], [18, 0, 18.712, 18.792, 19.412, 0, 24000, 0], [19, 0, 19.712, 19.789, 20.432, 0, 24000, 0], [20, 0, 20.712, 20.797, 21.465, 0, 24000, 0], [21, 0, 21.712, 21.797, 22.534, 0, 24000, 0], [22, 0, 22.712, 22.795, 23.559, 0, 24000, 0], [23, 0, 23.712, 23.796, 24.505, 0, 24000, 0], [24, 0, 24.712, 24.798, 25.627, 0, 24000, 0], [25, 0, 25.712, 25.793, 26.463, 0, 24000, 0], [26, 0, 26.712, 26.788, 27.561, 0, 24000, 0], [27, 0, 27.712, 27.795, 28.431, 0, 24000, 0], [28, 0, 28.712, 28.8, 29.528, 0, 24000, 0], [29, 0, 29.712, 29.796, 30.789, 0, 24000, 0], [30, 0, 30.712, 30.872, 31.881, 0, 24000, 0], [31, 0, 31.712, 31.959, 32.931, 0, 24000, 0], [32, 0, 32.712, 33.013, 34.051, 0, 24000, 0], [33, 0, 33.712, 34.135, 34.948, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 16.712, "last_real_feed_done": 16.787, "onset": 17.268, "gate_read_done": 17.268, "fire": null, "candidate_first_pcm": null, "stall_note": null, "stall_first_pcm": null, "local_first_pcm": 17.268, "wait_start": null, "expert_req": null, "expert_resp": null, "relay_synth_start": null, "relay_first_pcm": null, "relay_synth_end": null, "first_any_pcm": 17.268, "first_answer_pcm": 17.268, "session_end": 34.948}, "ttfa_answer_s": 0.556, "ttfa_any_s": 0.556}
{"id": "q0237", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 498313030, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "(a) A 4-pole machine has lap winding with 36 winding elements. What are the back and front pitches of this winding, expressed in commutator bars? (b) A 4-pole machine has wave winding with 37 winding elements. What are the three pitches of this winding expressed in commutator bars?\n\nA. Back pitch for lap winding is 12, front pitch is 13. Back pitch for wave winding is 7, front pitch is 6 or 7.\nB. Back pitch for lap winding is 9, front pitch is 10. Back pitch for wave winding is 9, front pitch is 8 or 9.\nC. Back pitch for lap winding is 8, front pitch is 9. Back pitch for wave winding is 10, front pitch is 11 or 12.\nD. Back pitch for both windings is 8, front pitch is 9 or 10.\nE. Back pitch for both windings is 9, front pitch is 11 or 12.\nF. Back pitch for lap winding is 11, front pitch is 9. Back pitch for wave winding is 10, front pitch is 8 or 9.\nG. Back pitch for lap winding is 7, front pitch is 6. Back pitch for wave winding is 11, front pitch is 12 or 13.\nH. Back pitch for lap winding is 10, front pitch is 8. Back pitch for wave winding is 9, front pitch is 9 or 10.\nI. Back pitch for lap winding is 10, front pitch is 11. Back pitch for wave winding is 8, front pitch is 7 or 8.\nJ. Back pitch for lap winding is 9, front pitch is 8. Back pitch for wave winding is 9, front pitch is 9 or 10.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0237.wav", "input_sha256": "34c9cf99c26283ae09c927156b9a703f99e4f843e2a93725b65beb63c90a7371", "input_samples": 1534600, "input_s": 95.912, "n_real_chunks": 96, "score": 0.7976, "act": 0.9979, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, let's break this down step by step. First, we need to recall the formulas for back and front pitches in both lap winding and wave winding for a four-pole machine. For a four-pole machine with m poles, the total number of commutator bars is 2m. So here, that would be 8 bars. Now, for lap winding, the back pitch yb is calculated as y b = z / p, where z is the number of winding elements divided by the number of poles p. But since we have 3 6 elements and 4 poles, z is actually equal to the number of conductors per pole per phase times something else. Wait, no, let' s re-examine. In lap wind ing, each parallel path has one winding element per pole pitch. The formula for back pitch in lap wind ing is typically yb = z / A, but more directly, for back pitch, it's often yb = m or close to it, but let's use standard values. Actually, for a four- pole machine with lap winding and 3 6 elements, the back pitch is usually yb = 12, which corresponds to half the pole pitch or something similar. Let me think again. The correct approach: For lap winding, the back pitch yb is generally equal to the number of commutator bars per pole, which for four poles would be 2 bars per pole segment, but wait, no. Standardly, back pitch yb for lap winding is calculated as yb = z / A, but if we assume A = 1 for simplicity in some contexts, but perhaps better to use known results. I recall that for a four-pole machine with lap winding and 36 elements, the back pitch is 12 commutator bars, and the front pitch is 13. That matches option A. Now for part B: wave winding with 37 elements. Wave winding has two pitches: back pitch y b and front pitch yf. The back pitch for wave winding is usually y b = z / 2, so 3 7 / 2 is not integer, but approximately 19, but that doesn't fit. Wait, no, for wave winding in a four-pole machine, the back pitch is often yb = m + 1 or something else. Let me recall: the three pitches", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 92, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 5603, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 79336, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0237_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "da127bb2ce8a2d023b1b00e3103d3bf636f8337fd7e3c3f803077616412b0cd6", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 60.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.073, 1.132, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.077, 2.137, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.08, 3.14, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.083, 4.148, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.078, 5.138, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.083, 6.148, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.078, 7.139, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.081, 8.145, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.076, 9.138, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.081, 10.143, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.085, 11.151, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.082, 12.141, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.083, 13.149, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.085, 14.152, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.081, 15.141, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.082, 16.146, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.074, 17.128, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.082, 18.147, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.084, 19.147, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.087, 20.154, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.085, 21.15, 1, 0, 0], [21, 1, 22.0, 22.086, 22.151, 1, 0, 0], [22, 1, 23.0, 23.085, 23.148, 1, 0, 0], [23, 1, 24.0, 24.079, 24.134, 1, 0, 0], [24, 1, 25.0, 25.082, 25.142, 1, 0, 0], [25, 1, 26.0, 26.087, 26.148, 1, 0, 0], [26, 1, 27.0, 27.088, 27.151, 1, 0, 0], [27, 1, 28.0, 28.089, 28.158, 1, 0, 0], [28, 1, 29.0, 29.087, 29.153, 1, 0, 0], [29, 1, 30.0, 30.084, 30.15, 1, 0, 0], [30, 1, 31.0, 31.086, 31.15, 1, 0, 0], [31, 1, 32.0, 32.083, 32.144, 1, 0, 0], [32, 1, 33.0, 33.083, 33.148, 1, 0, 0], [33, 1, 34.0, 34.083, 34.148, 1, 0, 0], [34, 1, 35.0, 35.087, 35.153, 1, 0, 0], [35, 1, 36.0, 36.083, 36.142, 1, 0, 